{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Men of blood</b> — who shed blood; they will hate the blameless one and kill him." "<b>They seek his life</b> — the life of the blameless one, and they will demand his blood. Another interpretation: his life is joined to one of the men of blood, and so it is, \"and the upright seek his life\" — a man of blood, to kill them because of the blameless one. Or the word \"his life\" is joined to one of \"and the upright,\" and the matter is doubled."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:22.119521991Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}